          },
          {
            "findingId": "SP-004",
            "reason": "Not a defect: the git init -b main on an existing repo-less directory is the plan-backed C19 behavior (repos.go:582-584 comment), is guarded (dir exists AND no .git), and git init is non-destructive/reversible (creates only .git, touches no existing files); the 'unconditional side effect, no confirmation' framing with a fix of merely 'add a UI note' identifies intended behavior, not a code defect — and misses the actual cataloged defects here (GV3-008 stray-.git ordering, GV3-194 spec deviation)."
          },
          {
            "findingId": "SP-005",
